'''Salora International Limited''' is an Indian conglomerate and the flagship company of the [[Jiwarajka Group]].<ref name="aboutus">[http://www.salora.com/About/Default.aspx "Salora: About Us"] {{webarchive|url=https://web.archive.org/web/20080322092809/http://www.salora.com/About/Default.aspx |date=2008-03-22 }}, Salora corporate website. Retrieved on 2008-05-03.</ref><ref>{{cite news |title=Salora International board recommends 45% dividend |url=http://www.myiris.com/newsCentre/newsPopup.php?fileR=20080429195423130&dir=2008/04/29&secID=livenews |publisher=IRIS Business Services |date=29 April 2008 |accessdate=2008-05-03 |url-status=dead |archiveurl=https://web.archive.org/web/20110714143413/http://www.myiris.com/newsCentre/newsPopup.php?fileR=20080429195423130&dir=2008%2F04%2F29&secID=livenews |archivedate=14 July 2011 }}</ref> Their business spans the complete [[supply chain]], and includes [[logistics]], [[Service (economics)|service]], [[manufacturing]] and [[Distribution (business)|distribution]].<ref name="aboutus" />

The company went [[public company|public]] in March 1993.<ref name="valuenotes1">[http://www.valuenotes.com/SChhabria/sc_salora_09dec05.asp?ArtCd=70792&Cat=C&Id=767 Salora International Ltd (Rs 109)] {{webarchive|url=https://web.archive.org/web/20070927193211/http://www.valuenotes.com/SChhabria/sc_salora_09dec05.asp?ArtCd=70792&Cat=C&Id=767 |date=2007-09-27 }}, valuenotes.com. Article dated 2005-09-12, retrieved 2007-03-13.</ref>

